---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { MANTIC, ORG } from "../../config";
---
<Base
  title={MANTIC.name}
  description="A new imprint from the Center for Innovating the Future. Books about the ideas changing what it means to be human."
>
  <header class="hband hband--amber">
    <div class="hbtext">
      <h1>{MANTIC.name}.</h1>
      <p>A new imprint from the Center, for arguments too long for an essay and too witty
      for a textbook.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead"><h2>What Mantic looks for.</h2></div>
      <div class="prin">
        <div class="pr">
          <h3>Ideas that demand permanence.</h3>
          <p>An argument that will still be worth reading in ten years, not a thesis timed to a news cycle.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pr">
          <h3>Authors willing to be held to them.</h3>
          <p>A book is a position with a name on it. Mantic publishes people who intend to defend theirs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pr">
          <h3>Subjects that change what being human means.</h3>
          <p>Technology, cognition, money, attention. The forces that alter people before anyone votes on them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="shead"><h2>Where it stands.</h2></div>
      <p class="dnote">
        Mantic has no list yet. The imprint was set up to publish the Center's long-form work
        and is commissioning its first titles now. It is building its own home at
        <a href={MANTIC.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">manticpublishing.com</a>.
        Writers with a manuscript that meets the three tests above can write to
        <a href={`mailto:${ORG.email}`}>{ORG.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
